# What the image is built from is small: src, web and the package files. The
# Dockerfile installs dependencies itself, so anything here that is already
# installed, generated, or written at runtime is both waste and a hazard.
#
# Runtime data, in particular, is written by the container as root — and an
# unreadable file does not merely bloat the upload, it aborts the build with
# "no permission to read from ...", which reads like a code problem and is not.

# Runtime data, owned by the container
config/
cache/
overlays/
*.log

# Installed, not copied — the image runs npm install itself
node_modules/
web/node_modules/
web/.svelte-kit/

# History and tooling
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.claude/

# A clone the update script leaves behind; building it into itself is a loop
Jellystreamerr/

# Local scratch
test/
docs/
*.md
!README.md
